From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:29:00 +0800
Subject: DmaBufAllocator: open the system heap read-only when read-write is
 refused

The Plasma container gets /dev/dma_heap/system with read access only (LXC device rule), and
allocation needs no more (DMA_HEAP_IOCTL_ALLOC works on a read-only descriptor). A read-write open
that fails with EACCES is retried read-only for the system heap.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-27
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [a container that grants the heap read-only]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:camera.frames (libcamera path: gap)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/48
---
 src/libcamera/dma_buf_allocator.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/dma_buf_allocator.cpp b/src/libcamera/dma_buf_allocator.cpp
index d8c62dd..d4aeb26 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/dma_buf_allocator.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/dma_buf_allocator.cpp
@@ -101,6 +101,8 @@ DmaBufAllocator::DmaBufAllocator(DmaBufAllocatorFlags type)
 			continue;
 
 		int ret = ::open(info.deviceNodeName, O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC, 0);
+		if (ret < 0 && errno == EACCES && info.type == DmaBufAllocatorFlag::SystemHeap)
+			ret = ::open(info.deviceNodeName, O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC, 0);
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			ret = errno;
 			LOG(DmaBufAllocator, Debug)
